    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Reading the traces",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 11
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Time**\nElapsed seconds from the first sample of each run.\n\n**Distance**\nOriginal CSV Distance in metres. A run needs a Distance channel for this view.\n\n**Compare**\nSelect a second imported run to overlay gray traces. Import another CSV to enable a meaningful comparison.\n\n**Channels**\nThe fixed traces use the sample's MoTeC names. Use Extra channel for other names; its units are shown in the selector.\n\n**Interaction**\nHover a trace for values. Grafana XY charts have independent cursors and zoom; linked MoTeC cursors and lap comparisons aren't included."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Lap durations - selected run",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "osprey_csv"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43,
        "w": 18,
        "h": 8
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "osprey_csv"
          },
          "rawSql": "WITH points AS (\n SELECT elapsed_s,\n max(value) FILTER (WHERE channel='Lap Number') AS lap,\n max(value) FILTER (WHERE channel='Lap Invalidated') AS invalid\n FROM samples WHERE run_id=(${run:sqlstring})::bigint AND channel IN ('Lap Number','Lap Invalidated')\n GROUP BY elapsed_s\n), boundaries AS (\n SELECT *, lag(lap) OVER (ORDER BY elapsed_s) AS previous_lap FROM points WHERE lap IS NOT NULL\n), segments AS (\n SELECT *, sum(CASE WHEN previous_lap IS DISTINCT FROM lap THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) OVER (ORDER BY elapsed_s) AS segment FROM boundaries\n), laps AS (\n SELECT segment, min(lap) AS lap, min(elapsed_s) AS start_s, max(elapsed_s) AS last_s,\n coalesce(max(invalid),0)>0 AS invalid FROM segments GROUP BY segment\n), durations AS (\n SELECT *, lead(start_s) OVER (ORDER BY segment)-start_s AS duration_s,\n lead(lap) OVER (ORDER BY segment) AS next_lap FROM laps\n), classified AS (\n SELECT *, coalesce(segment>1 AND next_lap=lap+1, false) AS complete FROM durations\n) SELECT lap::integer AS \"Lap\",\nCASE WHEN complete THEN round(duration_s::numeric,3)::double precision END AS \"Duration (s)\",\nCASE WHEN complete THEN to_char(duration_s * interval '1 second','MI:SS.MS') END AS \"Lap time\",\nCASE WHEN NOT complete THEN 'Partial' WHEN invalid THEN 'Invalid' ELSE 'Complete' END AS \"Status\",\nround((last_s-start_s)::numeric,3)::double precision AS \"Recorded span (s)\"\nFROM classified ORDER BY segment",
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "cellHeight": "sm"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
       }
    }
  ]
